Runbox.el - [Run] in Tool[Box]
******************************

Runbox provides TRAMP-redirected variants of common Emacs commands (e.g.
‘runbox-shell’ for ‘shell’, ‘runbox-eglot’ for ‘eglot’) that spawn their
subprocess in a different environment than the one implied by the
current local buffer.

   For example, it is possible to open a buffer for file
‘/home/user/MyProject/main.c’ and issue a ‘compile’ command or spawn the
Eglot LSP client as if it was a
‘/toolbox:Fedora:/home/user/MyProject/main.c’ buffer whilst remaining on
the non-remote buffer.

     *Note:* This package is ALPHA stage software.  It has not been
     tested thoroughly and bugs are likely to occur.

   The main use case of this package is to transparently run LSP
clients, shells, compilation commands, etc.  against binaries residing
in Toolbox (https://containertoolbx.org/) containers while operating in
a local buffer.  It generalizes to any TRAMP backend that operates
similarly and has a 1:1 mapping with the host's home directory, such as
the backend for Distrobox (https://distrobox.it/) or fphost
(https://github.com/antrmn/tramp-flatpak-host) (which runs commands
outside the Flatpak sandbox).

